    "evidence_text": " Matt Rogers co-wrote the song, while Ross Copperman co-produced the song with Eldredge.\n\n Eldredge wrote the song with Ross Copperman.\n\nBrett Eldredge\n\nBrett Ryan Eldredge (born March 23, 1986) is an American country music singer, songwriter and record producer, signed to Atlantic Records Nashville.\n\n Her songs have been featured on the TV show \"Nashville\" and recorded by Keith Urban, Brett Eldredge, Sara Evans, Eli Young Band, Maddie & Tae, and more.\n\n She is now a staff writer at Sony ATV Music, and had her first number 1 single in June 2014 with Brett Eldredge's \"Beat of the Music\".\n\n Eldredge co-wrote the song with Chris DeStefano and Ashley Gorley.\n\n Eldredge wrote the song with Ross Copperman and Scooter Carusoe.\n\nChris DeStefano\n\nChristopher Michael \"Chris\" DeStefano is a Grammy Award Winning American singer/songwriter, record producer and multi instrumentalist, raised in Mt. Laurel, New Jersey and currently residing in Nashville, Tennessee.\n\n Eldredge wrote the song with Jon Nite and Greg Becker.",
